// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - NobleSavageSouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P2232927115" "The Only Good Day Was Yesterday"
// tDetailString :
"P4003061759" "It started as a simple scavenger mission&<br><br><b><color deepskyblue>The Only Good Day Was Yesterday</color></b><br><br>...insofar as anything in First Ward is simple, at least. Soon, however, it became clear that D.U.S.T. had a crisis on its hands in the Free-Fire Zone. But after investigating several of their facilities, which were overrun with mutated Seers called the Awakened and the angry spirits of the Apparitions, it started to get...unclear. Noble Savage, the new Hetman of the Compound, decided to bring in an expert on psychic phenomena and sent you to recruit Katie Douglas, perhaps more famously known as Seer 1381. But you weren't the only one looking for Katie. An Apparition, known only as the 'Surgeon', had piggybacked along with you, and now that you had led him to Katie he wanted to claim her for himself. Free of the Surgeon's influence you were able to dispatch the thing, though it didn't do much in the way of making a good first impression."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1495962982" "It started as a simple scavenger mission, insofar as anything in First Ward is simple, at least. Soon, however, it became clear that D.U.S.T. had a crisis on its hands in the Free-Fire Zone."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P31377100" "It started as a simple scavenger mission, insofar as anything in First Ward is simple, at least. Soon, however, it became clear that D.U.S.T. had a crisis on its hands in the Free-Fire Zone. But after investigating several of their facilities, which were overrun with mutated Seers called the Awakened and the angry spirits of the Apparitions, it started to get...unclear."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3954519788" "It started as a simple scavenger mission, insofar as anything in First Ward is simple, at least. Soon, however, it became clear that D.U.S.T. had a crisis on its hands in the Free-Fire Zone. But after investigating several of their facilities, which were overrun with mutated Seers called the Awakened and the angry spirits of the Apparitions, it started to get...unclear. Noble Savage, the new Hetman of the Compound, decided to bring in an expert on psychic phenomena and sent you to recruit Katie Douglas, perhaps more famously known as Seer 1381."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DamagedScanner 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2581232721" "Signal Drop"
// DetailString :
"P522249297" "The Compound made sure their scavenger team had a tracer-beacons with them, but their last tac-scanner has seen better days. According to its readings, though, whatever remains of the scavenger team is still at the D.U.S.T. munitions depot."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Ghostband 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2187321511" "The Ghostband"
// DetailString :
"P3589386323" "Noble Savage gave you a ghostband transceiver that will allow you both a semblance of contact while you're in ARCLIGHT. He'll help you as best he can while you attempt to temporarily bypass the facility's Black Channeled communications network. From the look of the ghostband transceiver, it looks like Gully has been working hard on the Compound's technical gadgets to shed some of the guilt he still has from abandoning his scavenger team in the FFZ."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BlackChannelClue01 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1015414635" "Compound Theory"
// DetailString :
"P4014771856" "From what you can piece together from ARCLIGHT's incoming transmissions, the Asylum ordered the retrieval of escaped Awakened from the Sunken City. The mission was a success, but shortly thereafter almost all of the D.U.S.T. facilities in or around the FFZ, including <color yellow>BETTERMOUSETRAP and D-SEC</color> were compromised by the Apparitions. And when that happened, the Asylum-- or more properly, Praetor Tilman-- enacted the Black Channel Protocols, which effectively cut all communications down across the organization."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BlackChannelClue02 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2487318655" "BETTERMOUSETRAP"
// DetailString :
"P3265082288" "This section of ARCLIGHT's outgoing logs is the most troubling: <color orange>'Our persona training is useless against these ghosts, especially when the Awakened keep hitting us with psychosocratic logic loops.'</color><br><br>If D.U.S.T. can be compromised so easily, what chance does the Compound have? When you're finished here, it looks like your next stop is the <color yellow>D.U.S.T. medical facility code-named BETTERMOUSETRAP</color> to see what their science teams discovered before the Black Channel cut them off from the rest of the Ward."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SurgeonClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1141676842" "The Residency"
// DetailString :
"P2496349919" "The possessed monstrosity that referred to itself as the <color red>'Surgeon'</color> was carrying a D.U.S.T. security clearance card. It identified the host body as one Dr. Jonas Fletcher, a graduate of the Neutropolis Academy of Applied Extragenics."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - YellingClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3814978089" "Anger Management"
// DetailString :
"P3949386446" "What's wrong with you? That's twice now you've yelled at someone like a lunatic. Is First Ward and its inherent insanity getting to you? Are you taking on too much? In your last outburst towards Candlestick, you even insulted him, calling him a freak. And while that's relative, you'd think with the kinds of people you run with, you'd be used to his... colorful appearance. Maybe you're just tired. That must be it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - WhereaboutsClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3441785381" "Office 1381"
// DetailString :
"P2821483400" "You spoke to Candlestick, a powerful psychic of the Carnival of Light, about the Awakened. He and his fellow psychics fear the monstrosities, refusing to probe the 'personasphere' too deep to learn about them. Candlestick did point you to Katie Douglas, however, the first Seer to escape the Seer Network in Praetoria proper. And it turns out that Katie Douglas is hiding out at Office 1381 here in First Ward. There's only one problem: Katie Douglas wants nothing to do with the Compound or the Carnival.<br><br>And what was that voice in your head just then?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PiggybackClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1025606455" "Piggyback"
// DetailString :
"P381561553" "You're hearing the Surgeon's voice in your head. Actually, you're hearing <i>two</i> : the voice of the now-dead, formerly-possessed Dr. Jonas Fletcher and whatever insane Apparition used his body as a host. Their thoughts and personalities have somehow merged...and attached themselves to <i>you.</i> <color red>You're starting to show the first signs of possession.</color> And you have no idea for a cure...outside of death."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - RelinquishedClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3341367603" "Unwanted Baggage"
// DetailString :
"P1380197045" "The Surgeon has relinquished his possession of you, his Apparition rushing to claim the soul of Katie Douglas!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - FlashbackLeft 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - PalatineSupplyCrisisDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1046803419" "{HeroName}, it warms my heart to see you again. So...what do you think of the new Hetman?"
// Answer Text :
"P4254443954" "Noble Savage is a bold choice. The Compound and the Forlorn are united."
// Page LikeSavagePage Text :
"P1963183561" "We are friends with the Carnival of Light again, as well. This unification came about only through your help, my friend, as did my crown. Your humility in these matters does you credit; indeed, all of First Ward is blessed to have found a protector in one like you. <br><br>What can I do for you now?"
// Answer Text :
"P3006110032" "Noble Savage mentioned the Compound is running short on supplies."
// Page ScavengerPage Text :
"P857512782" "We are, as are the Forlorn. The first scavenger teams found little to bring back, though they did not sortie far. The last team felt the mounting desperation, and perhaps this is why they are lost."
// Answer Text :
"P3270749269" "Savage mentioned that one returned."
// Page FFZPage Text :
"P1283524800" "Yes, a Forlorn named Gully. His team was so bold as  to enter the Free-Fire Zone to accomplish their mission. And though I advised that they use the Shadowed Paths, they abandoned them for reasons that are still unclear. He is shaken by the experience and, though Noble wants me to, I have not the heart to press the matter just yet.<br><br><color orange>See if you can find out what happened to the scavenger team, {HeroName}.</color> You should know... this Gully <i>sees you as his savior.</i>  Perhaps he will open up to you."
// Answer Text :
"P3817805547" "I'll talk to Gully and find out what happened."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - GullySupplyCrisisDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P314181492" "{HeroName}, it is an honor to meet you. I am Gully, recently returned from the feral red haze of...of, well, my previous....<br><br>I guess I  don't have to think about <i>that</i>  anymore, thanks to your efforts with Dr. Helix."
// Answer Text :
"P1144393910" "Tell me what happened to your scavenger team, Gully."
// Page LikeGhoulsPage Text :
"P3473104151" "I am. I...and I must admit something to you, {Hero.gender=male good sir|milady}. The Genetic Resequencer restored my mind, but it also restored my cowardice. I'm afraid that I abandoned my cohorts shortly after we got into the FFZ. We were using the Shadowed Paths to raid a D.U.S.T. munitions depot when...when something went wrong."
// Answer Text :
"P2366601043" "What exactly went wrong?"
// Page WentWrongPage Text :
"P2426671861" "The Shadowed Paths <i>weren't</i>  safe, at least not for us, and contrary to all the stories we have heard. The scavenger team came under attack by an <color red>Apparition</color> and I ran for my life. When I stepped back into the real Ward, <i>even more</i> Apparitions swirled about me, running rampant through the FFZ."
// Answer Text :
"P3279812737" "And what about D.U.S.T.? They control the Free-Fire Zone."
// Page DUSTPage Text :
"P2618897793" "Not anymore, not from what I saw. <color red>D.U.S.T. soldiers</color> were firing on one another all in a panic. When I saw an Apparition possess one of them, I knew why.<br><br><color orange>The Free-Fire Zone has been compromised by the Apparitions and what remains of the scavenger team is trapped there.</color><br><br>Here, take this, it's the same kind of tac-scanner that you used before...only it's still pretty busted up from the battle with the old Hetman. I've tried to repair it, though, and key it to the frequencies of my... of my old team members."
// Answer Text :
"P1241844757" "I'll pick up their trail and find what's happened to them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P447962865" "The former Hetman's military uprising left both the Forlorn and the Compound in dire need of supplies; our defenses, weapons, and rations are depleted at levels that discomfort me. To this end, the Palatine and I have been sending out scavenger teams into the Ward, but they have met with little success. <br><br><color orange>Our last scavenger team never returned and I'd like you to find out what happened to them. And to bring back whatever they were after.</color><br><br>Well...one of them <i>did</i>  return-- named <color yellow>Gully</color>-- but he's one of the <i>new</i> Forlorn, his mind just recently restored. He's only managed to give the Palatine and I scattered details of what happened. <color orange>Start by speaking with the Palatine</color>...I think Gully's too afraid of upsetting me to give his full report."
// AcceptString :
"P2312777089" "I'll speak to Anna about the lost scavenger team."
// SendOffString :
"P3400512933" "Good. I would have her advice both as my Palatine and someone that has traveled First Ward far and wide through the Shadowed Paths. Her insight is a rare thing... very rare indeed."
// TaskTitle :
"P1149569429" "<color deepskyblue>The Only Good Day Was Yesterday</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P352774039" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: Ashes to Ashes</color>"

