// Dialog :
"P3471439962" "You find an assortment of high-impact rounds, a few thump grenades, and a few special-issue D.U.S.T. micromunitions that might be able to be retrofitted for the Last Worders' weapons."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - ScriptAmmoStolen2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P308053271" "This ammunitions cache is devoid of anything useful. It looks like it's been ransacked recently by the D.U.S.T. Rangers currently battling their possessed cell members."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2953928650" "While you managed to find the surviving members of the lost scavenger team, it looks like the Free-Fire Zone has more problems than a few Last Worders trying to steal some food and supplies from the area. A D.U.S.T. munitions depot was infested with Apparitions and Possessed. The whole of the D.U.S.T. Cell was in disarray, firing on their former allies."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBeginFlashback 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P130485241" "Your report of the Free-Fire Zone is troubling, {HeroName}. I've seen the Apparitions only from afar, or when my diagnostics deem it essential for my mortal mind to dream. <br><br>I'm surprised that D.U.S.T. can't hold the Apparitions off. They're crack troops, with persona safeguard training. That you saw so many of them possessed...we're missing something here, but I have some suspicions on where to start looking for possible answers. None of it negates resupply of the Compound, however."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MuldoonDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P39221502" "{HeroName}, it's me, Captain Muldoon! You spared my life, and the lives of my men, back when we first met."
// Answer Text :
"P2285223532" "What are you doing here, Captain?"
// Page MuldoonAlivePage Text :
"P2656089451" "Paying off that debt. Now, listen: I've been scouting around the whole of the FFZ. I've been witness to lots of strange and evil stuff regarding the Apparitions and its disruption of D.U.S.T's special operations branches.<br><br>During all the in-fighting, I may have lost my whole cell. Things have gone from bad to worse, but this science lab should have some answers on how we might be able to stop it, or cure it, or contain it. Let's find out."
// Answer Text :
"P1919903555" "Let's go."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ArrayDialog1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Inaccessible Text :
"P3452560118" "<color orange>Black Channel Protocols in effect. No access to this terminal is authorized.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2141117208" "Leave."
// Page Override Text :
"P1188317022" "<color orange>Black Channel Protocols temporary bypass: Some archived transmissions corrupted. This comm station array only contains the last incoming transmissions from ARCLIGHT. For last outgoing transmissions, please try another terminal.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2879268173" "(Check last incoming transmissions.)"
// Page DataDownloaded Text :
"P2295752255" "<color orange>All archived ARCLIGHT incoming transmissions have been downloaded.</color>"
// Page LastReceivedPage1 Text :
"P1344179384" "<color yellow>PROJECT ARCLIGHT: Transmissions Log [Incoming]</color><br><br>Colonel Vargas, CO D-SEC, to Captain Jennings, CO ARCLIGHT<br><br>Captain, our Mother just called. It seems some very special Seers either escaped or were broken out of the Asylum recently. Current reports from the cell Captains in the FFZ pinpoint them as being in the Sunken City. I need you to send a squadron out and retrieve them. Bring the Seers back to ARCLIGHT and contain them until further orders. Be advised, the Asylum are referring to these Seers as 'Awakened', but I have no idea what that means. Evidently, they exhibit strange mutations, often physical, and give off a psychic resonance quite unlike the Seers we are familiar with. Your men should have ample enough persona psychic defense training to deal with them, but the Asylum notes that these 'Awakened' may put up a fight. Under no circumstances are you to damage the package. This comes from on high. We mustn't disappoint Her. Vargas out."
// Answer Text :
"P3115737133" "(Keep scanning last incoming transmissions)"
// Page LastReceivedPage2 Text :
"P668146060" "<color yellow>PROJECT ARCLIGHT: Transmissions Log [Incoming]</color><br><br>Colonel Vargas, CO D-SEC, to Captain Jennings, CO ARCLIGHT<br><br>Well done, Captain. I've relayed your success to the Asylum. They should be sending out one of own their spec-ops teams to ARCLIGHT for immediate exfil of the package. Between you and me, I really hope it's not the IDF, or this thing is going to move from Strange Request to Something Really Bad Happened. Vargas out."
// Answer Text :
"P1272551137" "(Keep scanning last received transmissions)"
// Page LastReceivedPage3 Text :
"P3599160222" "<color yellow>PROJECT ARCLIGHT: Transmissions Log [Incoming]</color><br><br>Colonel Vargas, CO D-SEC, to all Cell Commanding Officers of special operations in First Ward<br><br>Be advised that the 'Awakened' are a Red-level threat. Shoot them on sight. They are also working with the Apparitions in the FFZ for reasons that remain unknown. Several D.U.S.T. soldiers have already been compromised, either through possession or mind-control. Shoot them on sight; they cannot be saved. We have our science team at BETTERMOUSETRAP looking into the hows and whys, but until you hear different, consider us at battle stations throughout the Ward. I have relayed all of this to the Asylum. When I hear from Mother, I will update you all. Stay safe and stay strong. We will get out of this. Vargas out."
// Page LastReceivedPage4 Text :
"P1136418492" "<color yellow>PROJECT ARCLIGHT: Transmissions Log [Incoming]</color><br><br>Colonel Vargas, CO D-SEC, to all Cell Commanding Officers in First Ward<br><br>Colonel Vargas to all D.U.S.T. special operatives through the Ward: ARCLIGHT is compromised. BETTERMOUSETRAP is compromised. The FFZ is a ghost zone. D-SEC? We have our own problems. The less I say about the Seer Network the better. Someone in Praetoria has just enacted the Black Channel Protocols. You all know what that means. We will be cut off from one another. Mother has decided to abandon her children.<br><br>The Black Channel is set to drop now,so I've got one chance to say it: There is no help coming. Repeat: there is no help <b><color orange>[transmission ends, presumably because the Black Channel Protocols went into effect]</color></b>"
// Answer Text :
"P184364601" "(Download files and leave)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ArrayDialog2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Override Text :
"P1652377468" "<color orange>Black Channel Protocols temporary bypass: Some archived transmissions corrupted. This comm station array only contains the last outgoing transmissions from ARCLIGHT. For last incoming transmissions, please try another terminal.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2095091352" "(Check last outgoing transmissions)"
// Page DataDownloaded Text :
"P208577848" "<color orange>All archived ARCLIGHT outgoing transmissions have been downloaded.</color>"
// Page LastSentPage1 Text :
"P3439533111" "<color yellow>PROJECT ARCLIGHT: Transmissions Log [Outgoing]</color><br><br>Captain Jennings, CO ARCLIGHT, to Colonel Vargas, CO D-SEC<br><br>Colonel, I'm happy to report that the 'Awakened' were retrieved from the Sunken City and brought back to ARCLIGHT as per your orders. The operation went smoother than expected, with no casualties, despite the warnings from the Asylum that the 'Awakened' may be unnaturally antagonistic in their confusion. Instead, they gave my men no trouble at all and came to ARCLIGHT willingly, as if they wanted our protection from the rest of First Ward. Mother should be pleased."
// Answer Text :
"P644768923" "(Keep scanning last sent transmissions)"
// Page LastSentPage2 Text :
"P2887664778" "<color yellow>PROJECT ARCLIGHT: Transmissions Log [Outgoing]</color><br><br>Captain Jennings, CO ARCLIGHT, to Colonel Vargas, CO D-SEC<br><br>The attack continues. These 'Awakened' are mind-controlling my men to wander into the FFZ and get possessed by Apparitions. ARCLIGHT is full of ghosts and these crazy Asylum Seers. Please send help, Colonel. I'm concerned that my whole cell will be compromised by nightfa<br><br><b>[transmission ends abruptly]</b>."
// Page LastSentPage3 Text :
"P3001451907" "<color yellow>PROJECT ARCLIGHT: Transmissions Log [Outgoing]</color><br><br>Major Loeb, (acting CO) ARCLIGHT, to Colonel Vargas, CO D-SEC<br><br>Captain Jennings was compromised, sir, and put down, but the Apparition inside him simply jumped to Specialist Holloway. There are only four of us left now. Our persona training is useless against these ghosts, especially when the Awakened keep hitting us with psychosocratic logic loops. I am hereby shutting ARCLIGHT down. Do not send help. Repeat: do not send help. I can already feel like I'm haunted in some way. I pray that the efforts at BETTERMOUSETRAP can find a way to end this.<br><br>Tell Mother we tried."
// Page LastSentPage4 Text :
"P3703567427" "<color yellow>PROJECT ARCLIGHT: Transmissions Log [Outgoing]</color><br><br>ARCLIGHT to Colonel Vargas, CO D-SEC<br><br>Loeb is one of them. Fields is one of them. No one can find Foster. Why aren't you responding to us, Colonel? Why are we going under Black Channel? Only Praetor Tilman can authorize that! I'm about to TOXIC AND GUTTED AND NO APOLOGIES oh no, I didn't say YOU WILL PAY US IN THE MEAT AND WE ALL HAVE UNFINISHED BUSINESS I'm not saying this <b><color orange>[transmission ends after the sound of a sidearm firing]</color></b>."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3477747921" "Theory time, {HeroName}. For years, D.U.S.T. has been using the Free-Fire Zone as a training ground, which loosely translates into live fire exercises against any and all targets that they can find there. They do this with the full but undisclosed support of some agency within the Cole regime back in Praetoria proper; one that funds them, equips them, and refills their ranks with fresh supersoldiers when necessary. They couldn't do this without being in contact with said agency.<br><br>Word from the FFZ is that a D.U.S.T. special operation science lab codenamed <color yellow>ARCLIGHT</color> suddenly went Black Channel. Either their comms are down or there's no one home. <color orange>Get into ARCLIGHT and find their communication records.</color> We need to know what D.U.S.T. has told its upper command about the situation here and if they ever got a response. Someone in Praetoria may have a way to contain the <color red>Apparitions</color>... or they may simply be sending in heavier forces. If things are <i>really</i>  bad, then they may just be abandoning their cells out here altogether. In any case, we can't afford to be in the dark."
// AcceptString :
"P1349543689" "We'll need something to bypass the Black Channel for this to work at all."
// SendOffString :
"P2025722355" "You're right. <color orange>When you're inside ARCLIGHT, find a way to temporarily override the communications lockdown. Here, take this ghostband transceiver with you.</color> With it, I'll be able to advise you from here. Good hunting, {HeroName}."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1730781383" "Search ARCLIGHT"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2005917730" "We've got to concentrate on ARCLIGHT right now, {HeroName}."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1945498192" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: What We Bring With Us</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P698049373" "For a brief moment, your ghostband transceiver explodes into a chorus of screams and commands that you cannot parse. The insidious power of the Apparitions is at work here."
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P2141125978" "Download files from Comm Station Array 01"
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P1421061785" "Download files from Comm Station Array 02"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2836457115" "Now you die!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3571567476" "Now we die..."
// Script Variable PET_NAME :
"P2601275127" "Captain Muldoon"
// Script Variable PET_DISPLAYINFO :
"P759175554" "Former D.U.S.T. Cell Commander"
// Script Variable PET_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2399942772" "<shout>Over here!"
// Script Variable SayOnRescue :
"P1875635026" "{HeroName}, it's me, Captain Muldoon!"
// Script Variable SayOnRecapture :
"P3805241234" "This is Muldoon, they got me cornered. Need assistance. Over."
// Script Variable SayOnRerescue :
"P2599116159" "You came back for me. Appreciated."
// Script Variable SayOnStranded :
"P3888988349" "I've lost your position. Over."
// Script Variable BOSS_1STBLOOD_DIALOG :
"P2556670503" "I'm under attack!"
// Script Variable BOSS_50HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P416405635" "I'm wounded!"
// Script Variable BOSS_25HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P1816971504" "My vitals are critical!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DEAD_DIALOG :
"P3514462294" "..."
// Script Variable BOSS_KILLEDHERO_DIALOG :
"P3770572925" "Target dropped."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P756096117" "Subjugator"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P1127431811" "Hello, {HeroName}."
// Script Variable PET_NAME :
"P3926237994" "Comm Array Station 01"
// Script Variable RescueObjectiveText :
"P360664393" "more comm arrays to access"
// Script Variable RescueObjectiveTextSingular :
"P2279585511" "Access the last comm array"
// Script Variable CAPTOR_ACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P4142343443" "<shout>Keep {Hero.gender=male him|her} away from this terminal!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1627440934" "<t=4 caption x= 0.2 y=0.5 d=4><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor purple>Noble Savage to {HeroName}: Who is that guy? And how does he know your name?"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1656907226" "<t=4 caption x= 0.3 y=0.3 d=4><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor purple>Fine, it's your call. If you want to take a D.U.S.T. Officer along with you, go right ahead."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P784832876" "<t=4 caption x= 0.2 y=0.5 d=4><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor purple>The Comm Channel Override should be coming up pretty soon. Get prepared. Everyone's going to know when you flip it."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3273822297" "<t=6 caption x= 0.3 y=0.3 d=6><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor purple>Good job, {HeroName}, hit those comm arrays now and download their logs. You'll have to get rid of any enemies protecting them first."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3255197282" "<t=6 caption x= 0.3 y=0.3 d=6><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor purple>Remember, {HeroName}, you need to bypass the Black Channel first to get access to these comm arrays."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3339401476" "<t=6 caption x= 0.3 y=0.3 d=6><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor purple>Noble Savage to {HeroName}: Take it easy in here. The ghostband is picking up multiple enemies."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2658075641" "<t=4 caption x= 0.3 y=0.3 d=4><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor purple>'Mother', huh? Of course she's involved. But what's her play?"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1199324602" "<t=8 caption x= 0.2 y=0.5 d=8><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor purple>So ARCLIGHT is ordered to secure these 'Awakened', something goes wrong, and Praetor Tilman cuts off all communications between D.U.S.T. spec-ops cells in First Ward. That's pretty severe, even for her."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2298676471" "<t=8 caption x= 0.3 y=0.3 d=8><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor purple>Noble Savage to {HeroName}: 'BETTERMOUSETRAP' is the code-name for a D.U.S.T. medical facility near ARCLIGHT. It sounds like these 'Awakened' somehow compromised most of D.U.S.T.'s operations in the FFZ. And we still have nothing to connect them to the Apparitions running around the rest of the Ward."

