// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P607749336" "You managed to enter ARCLIGHT and temporarily bypass the communications blackout long enough to download transmissions sent to and from various D.U.S.T. spec-ops cells in the Free-Fire Zone."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3485877637" "We'll get Gully and some of our more technical guys on these data retrievals, {HeroName}, but it's pretty evident that ARCLIGHT's last operation was a disaster. <i>And</i>  that the next step is the BETTERMOUSETRAP medical facility. The Asylum is certainly frightened of these <color red>'Awakened'</color>.... enough for Praetor Tilman to condemn the very soldiers that reported their existence. We're going to need to stretch our resources even further."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MedicalRecordsDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page AlreadyHaveRecordsPage Text :
"P2148575707" "<color orange>You already have copies of all pertinent and available medical transcripts regarding the Awakened.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"
// Page OpeningPage Text :
"P3952740641" "<color orange>You find a series of local medical transcripts regarding the Awakened Seers</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2285252735" "(Scan the report on their first appearance)"
// Page GeneralNaturePage Text :
"P3094236782" "<color yellow>Dr. Jonas Fletcher, Field Surgeon in Residence to D.U.S.T. special operations in First Ward, BETTERMOUSETRAP</color><br><br>Just before the Black Channel fell, Colonel Vargas, the CO of D-SEC, ordered one of our squadrons from BETTERMOUSETRAP to capture as many of the the Seer-subjects designated 'Awakened' as we could. What started as a seemingly innocuous request from Mother has turned into a four-alarm fire. But that's not really the point of these reports. Forgive me. The stress is getting to all of us.<br><br>We did not suspect any associations between the Awakened and the Apparitions at the time ARCLIGHT was sent to the Sunken City, and still do not have any verifiable evidence to support such a claim.<br><br>What we <b>do</b> know is that the presence of the Awakened caused nearly <b>all</b> of the Seers attached to the D.U.S.T. cells here in First Ward to turn on us, as well. The current theory is that the Awakened carry some kind of 'psychic contagion' which normally healthy Seers can catch, and readily so. Again, what any of this has to do with the Apparitions is still under investigation."
// Answer Text :
"P1313405741" "(Scan diagnosis reports on Awakened mutations)"
// Page PossibleCausesPage Text :
"P1631545050" "<color yellow>Dr. Jonas Fletcher, Field Surgeon in Residence to D.U.S.T. special operations in First Ward, BETTERMOUSETRAP</color><br><br>The mutations that manifest in the Awakened seem to be psychomorphic in nature, indicative of exposure to enormous amounts of Nth-Gen psychic stress. Though we do not have an exact pattern yet, these mutations come in degrees of physical severity, from barely noticeable to almost supraterrestrial-level physiology. Whatever the pattern, the severity of physical mutations in Awakened do not seem to correspond to their levels of psychic power. The reasons for this are currently unknown.<br><br>We may never make the connection between the Awakened and the Apparitions. Once our initial reports were sent to Colonel Vargas at D-SEC, who then relayed such findings to the Asylum, it resulted in an immediate call for Black Channel Protocols across all D.U.S.T. special operations in First Ward."
// Answer Text :
"P3586829034" "(Scan purpose of the Black Channel Protocols)"
// Page BlackChannelPage Text :
"P4247544483" "<color yellow>Dr. Jonas Fletcher, Field Surgeon in Residence to D.U.S.T. special operations in First Ward, BETTERMOUSETRAP</color><br><br>Mother has deemed that this secret medical facility be condemned and quietly disappeared. How nice. The Black Channel will lock us all down, so I fear this may be my last report. In that case, I would like to formally put, on the record, that I believe that a <i>magician</i>  should've been sent here instead of a doctor. The Awakened I can work on-- correction, <i>could</i>  have worked on had the Asylum given us adequate protection-- but just what am I supposed to do about the Apparitions? What advice can I give that doesn't end up straying into the occult, a subject I never studied? How am I supposed to perform an autopsy on a <i>ghost?</i>"
// Answer Text :
"P1870400773" "(Download all pertinent medical reports)"
// Page ExitPage Text :
"P3939481794" "<color orange>You have copies of all pertinent and available medical transcripts regarding the Awakened Seers.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P318485199" "So we know that a different spec-ops team from D.U.S.T. took some Awakened to the medical facility codenamed BETTERMOUSETRAP. According to the files you brought back, they were hoping to use its equipment to figure out how the Awakened could take over their Seers so easily... and whether there's any kind of procedure to remove or prevent it. <color orange>We need to know if D.U.S.T. has any medical records on file regarding the Awakened and, if so, we need to retrieve them.</color><br><br>Trust me, once those psychic monstrosities are done with D.U.S.T. they're going to move out into the rest of First Ward. The Compound simply can't handle them."
// AcceptString :
"P361920125" "I'll find whatever medical records are there."
// SendOffString :
"P262267036" "I hate to ask this of you, {HeroName}, but <color orange>I need you to bring back any medical supplies you can find, as well.</color> And one more thing: that ghostband transceiver we used at ARCLIGHT? Well, turns out that all its time in proximity to those Apparitions in there fried it. Gully has no idea why, but you're going to be without my help on this one."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3070541087" "Search BETTERMOUSETRAP"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1572974670" "{HeroName}, get your head in the game. I need you to retrieve any medical records D.U.S.T. may have on the Awakened."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1397789713" "<color deepskyblue>Part Three: Visitation Rites</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P4006011973" "It looks like D.U.S.T. abandoned this medical facility. The unnerving sensation of the Awakened moving freely about may explain why."
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P3907973713" "Download Awakened medical records"
// Script Variable PATROLLER1_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P2879822875" "I can sense an intruder.<t 2>And a powerful one, this time. That's...good."
// Script Variable PATROLLER1_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P1798705320" "The intruder is searching for something."
// Script Variable PATROLLER2_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P1093890316" "<t 2><t 2>It's searching for why we exist. Just like Fletcher did."
// Script Variable PATROLLER1_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P3117620511" "It has seen Awakened before."
// Script Variable PATROLLER2_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P1370025199" "<t 2><t 2>Correction: it has destroyed Awakened before."
// Script Variable HOSTAGE_NAME :
"P1279430546" "Medical Records Terminal"
// Script Variable CAPTOR_NAME :
"P1266328889" "Conduit"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P613208175" "Mindstorm"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - ScriptRescuedMainframe 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P3343103732" "Access the Medical Records Terminal"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3580846970" "The Surgeon"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2555045538" "<shout>VISITING HOURS ARE OVER!"
// Script Variable BOSS_1STBLOOD_DIALOG :
"P2386638835" "<shout>THOSE WERE CLASSIFIED FILES!<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable BOSS_75HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P1655093050" "<shout>We're losing him!<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable BOSS_50HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P1453375251" "If you could hand me the tyndallers, please.<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable BOSS_25HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P2806213040" "This was only supposed to be a residency!<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable BOSS_DEAD_DIALOG :
"P741071871" "<shout>I'll find another host! You just watch me!<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable BOSS_KILLEDHERO_DIALOG :
"P2297035647" "<em victory>Flatline!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1738482053" "Nevermind"

